; tiles.xon -- the delve set drawn, for a windowed front-end: a worked
; coal pit, stopped three weeks, its water rising.  Soot, wet rock,
; old timber and rust; what the men left lying where they left it.
;
; Read by the graphical front-end only: the set itself is the .xon files
; one directory up, and this directory is not one of them.
;
; (size W H) is every tile's size in pixels.  (colour "C" R G B [A]) names
; a colour by one character; A is 255 unless given, and 0 is clear.
; (tile NAME . PROPS) draws NAME: a glyph name (wall, player, potion, ...)
; or a creature's name.  (rows "..." ...) is the picture, one string a
; row, one character a pixel; (as OTHER) draws NAME as OTHER; (band
; "BAND") makes it that band's, in front of the set's.  Several tiles of
; one name are its variants: a cell takes one by its place, the same
; every time, (weight N) of them for each 1 of a tile without one.
; (part P) is one piece of a tile drawn by its neighbours: a wall's top,
; face, rims and corners, the shade a face casts on the floor.
; (light R G B N) makes a tile give light of that colour, N cells out;
; (flicker P) makes it waver by P percent, as a flame does.
; Anything with no tile is drawn as its glyph in the font.

(size 16 16)

(colour "." 0 0 0 0)
(colour "k" 33 25 22)
